# One line per site: "<name> <repo-url> [branch]".
# Consumed by `provision-all` / `deploy-all`. Blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored. branch is optional — omit it to track
# whatever the remote's default branch is; when given, it's passed as
# `provision --branch`, which persists as an operator-side setting (not
# written into the repo) — see README "Default branch".
#
# example-client git@github.com:youragency/example-client.git
# other-client    git@github.com:youragency/other-client.git      develop
